	abstract = {The automobile sector has been transformed by the fast pace of technical development of digital technologies, posting e-business as the driver of growth, efficiency, and sustainability. The effect of e-business adoption on business performance, customer engagement, and ecological sustainability in the automobile sector has been the interest of this study. By means of a well-structured survey of 80 respondents including sole proprietors, partnership firms and corporate entities, the research identifies the effectiveness of digital strategies like social media marketing, search engine optimisation (SEO), customer data management, and e-logistics. Results show that electronic business improves market access, efficiency of processes, client retention, and at the same time reduces operational costs and environmental impact. Still, widespread adoption is stymied by barriers such as tech limits, employee resistance, financial constraints and regulations. In conclu-sion, a fusion of digital and traditional businesses is the key to sustainable growth as per the paper. The findings offer important insights to automobile sector stakeholders, government policy makers, researchers, and technology providers seeking to optimise the e-business strategy for sustainable long term business growth. © 2025, Scibulcom Ltd.. All rights reserved.},
