	abstract = {In contrast with single-purpose mobile apps, super apps provide multiple diversified services that address a broad range of user needs. As it is relatively nascent, further research is required to determine the antecedents of continuance intention toward super apps. Therefore, a research model was developed by integrating an extended Mobile Expectation-Confirmation Model and multidimensional concept of relationship quality. The Partial Least Square-Structural Equation Modeling and Necessary Condition Analysis were used to analyze 494 responses which were collected in Malaysia and Taiwan. The results revealed that except for the relationship between enjoyment and continuance intention, all other relationships were significant for both countries. Practically, this study offers insights to enhance the development and localization strategies for super app service providers. Theoretically, this study extends the literature by utilizing a multi-analytical cross-country approach to investigate continuance intention toward super apps with an integrated research model. © 2025 International Association for Computer Information Systems.},
