	abstract = {Using data from publicly listed firms in China from 2008 to 2022, this paper examines the green spillover effects of customer firms’ digital transformation on suppliers’ environmental performance from a supply chain perspective. The results show that customer firms’ digital transformation improves suppliers’ environmental awareness and performance by enhancing supply chain transparency and alleviating financial constraints. This effect is particularly significant in state-owned enterprises, firms with high supplier concentration, low-pollution firms, and high-tech industries. In contrast, high supplier and customer concentration weaken these effects by reducing competitive pressures and innovation incentives. Supply chain transaction costs and geographical distance dampen this green spillover effect. © 2025 Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.},
